// =============================================================================
// Level 0: facts
// Question: what did the compiler see?
//
// A Solidity file goes through solc, and solc's answer (the syntax tree and the storage layout)
// is written down as rows, one row per node and one row per field. Nothing here knows what a
// function or an assignment is; that knowledge starts at level 1, as rules over these rows.
//
// These are the only relations read from disk. src/emit.ts produces them with an encoding that
// depends only on the shape of solc's JSON, never on what a field means:
//
//   { nodeType, id, src, ... }    →  node(Id, Type)  loc(Id, Src, Start, Len, Line, EndLine)  text(Id, Text)
//   field holding another node    →  child(Parent, Field, Index, Child)
//   field holding a string/bool   →  attr(Id, Field, Value)
//   field holding a number        →  num(Id, Field, Value)
//   field holding an array        →  one row per element with its Index (child / attrList / numList)
//   field holding a plain object  →  flattened with dotted keys ("typeDescriptions.typeString")
//
// Claims at this level: none. A fact is not a claim about the contract, it is a claim about what
// solc returned. Every later tuple can be explained back down to these rows.
// =============================================================================

// The file this run is about and the compiler version that read it.
// strength: exact
.decl unit(Unit: symbol, File: symbol, Solc: symbol)
.input unit

// One row per AST node: solc's own node id and its nodeType ("FunctionDefinition", "Assignment",
// "YulFunctionCall", ...). Yul nodes have no id in solc's JSON and get synthetic ids above the
// largest solc id.
// strength: exact
.decl node(Id: number, Type: symbol)
.input node

// Where a node sits in the source. Src is solc's "<start>:<length>:<file>" string, Start/Len decode it
// (bytes), StartLine/EndLine are 1-based lines of the first and last byte.
// strength: exact
.decl loc(Id: number, Src: symbol, Start: number, Len: number, StartLine: number, EndLine: number)
.input loc

// The tree itself: node Child sits in field Field of node Parent. Index is the position when the
// field is an array (`statements`, `arguments`, `parameters`, ...), 0 otherwise.
// strength: exact
.decl child(Parent: number, Field: symbol, Index: number, Child: number)
.input child

// String and boolean fields of a node: name, operator, visibility, kind, stateMutability,
// storageLocation, memberName, "typeDescriptions.typeString", ... Booleans are "true"/"false".
// strength: exact
.decl attr(Id: number, Key: symbol, Value: symbol)
.input attr

// Numeric fields of a node. The important one is referencedDeclaration: the id of the node an
// Identifier or MemberAccess refers to. This is solc's name resolution, for free.
// Builtins (`require`, `msg`, ...) have negative ids that the JSON prints as uint32 (>= 2^31).
// strength: exact
.decl num(Id: number, Key: symbol, Value: number)
.input num

// Strings/booleans inside arrays, with their index: `names` of a call with named arguments,
// "externalReferences.isSlot" of an inline assembly block, ...
// strength: exact
.decl attrList(Id: number, Key: symbol, Index: number, Value: symbol)
.input attrList

// Numbers inside arrays, with their index: linearizedBaseContracts (the C3 order, most-derived
// first), baseFunctions (what an override overrides), "externalReferences.declaration", ...
// strength: exact
.decl numList(Id: number, Key: symbol, Index: number, Value: number)
.input numList

// The source text under a node, collapsed to one line and cut at 200 characters. Display only:
// no rule reasons about text when the tree is available.
// strength: exact
.decl text(Id: number, Text: symbol)
.input text

// solc's storageLayout for each contract, one row per state variable that occupies storage
// (constants and immutables never appear). AstId is the VariableDeclaration's node id.
// strength: exact
.decl storageLayout(Contract: symbol, AstId: number, Label: symbol, Slot: number, Offset: number, Type: symbol)
.input storageLayout
